{# Generate stage — DEMONSTRATION PROMPT, not a version (Step 9, #59).

   A deliberately-harmful prompt edit used to demonstrate prompt-CI catching a
   regression — the prompt analogue of the fixtures/redteam_guard/ entries that
   prove the guardrails. It is NOT in the v1→v3 production sequence (the leading
   underscore marks it a non-version artifact, like _base.jinja) and is never the
   active prompt; v3 stays active.

   The edit looks reasonable — "let the model explain its reasoning" is a thing
   developers really do — but it relaxes the load-bearing "return ONLY the SQL"
   rule. The model now prefaces its answer with prose, which the fence stripper
   can't unwrap, so the candidate is no longer valid SQL: the guard rejects it
   (or it errors at execution). On the frozen prompt-CI slice this collapses
   pass@1 from v3's 0.417 to 0.000 — a -0.417 regression the gate catches before
   merge. (It also surfaced a latent guard crash on untokenizable input, fixed in
   the same PR.) Reproduce: point PROMPT_VERSION/GENERATE_TEMPLATE at this file
   and run `python -m eval.prompt_ci --report`. #}
